{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01FEHe6tSV4rVK7U9BMqZ4Fx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#ifndef MATRIX_H\n2\t#define MATRIX_H\n3\t\n4\t#ifdef __cplusplus\n5\textern \"C\" {\n6\t#endif\n7\t\n8\t#include <stddef.h>\n9\t#include <stdint.h>\n10\t\n11\t#define TRANSFORM_COUNT 3\n12\t\n13\t/**\n14\t * @brief Represents a square 2D matrix.\n15\t *\n16\t * This structure encapsulates a 2D matrix with its dimensions and data.\n17\t *\n18\t * @param dim The dimension (number of rows/columns) of the matrix.\n19\t * @param data Pointer to the array storing the matrix elements in row-major\n20\t * order.\n21\t */\n22\ttypedef struct {\n23\t  size_t dim;     //!< The dimension (number of rows/columns) of the matrix.\n24\t  uint64_t *data; //!< Pointer to the array storing the matrix elements in\n25\t                  //!< row-major order.\n26\t} Matrix2D;\n27\t\n28\ttypedef int (*Transformer)(Matrix2D *m, Matrix2D *invm, uint64_t mod);\n29\t\n30\t/**\n31\t * @brief Represents a 3D matrix.\n32\t *\n33\t * This structure encapsulates a 3D matrix with its dimensions and data.\n34\t *\n35\t * @param data Pointer to the array storing the 2D matrices.\n36\t * @param size The size (number of 2D matrices) in the 3D matrix.\n37\t */\n38\ttypedef struct {\n39\t  Matrix2D *data; //!< Pointer to the array storing the 2D matrices.\n40\t  size_t size;    //!< The size (number of 2D matrices) in the 3D matrix.\n41\t} Matrix3D;\n42\t\n43\t/**\n44\t * @brief Get a 2D matrix from a 3D matrix.\n45\t *\n46\t * This function retrieves a pointer to a 2D matrix from the specified index of\n47\t * the 3D matrix.\n48\t *\n49\t * @param lambda Pointer to the 3D matrix.\n50\t * @param idx The index of the desired 2D matrix.\n51\t *\n52\t * @return Pointer to the specified 2D matrix.\n53\t */\n54\tMatrix2D *matrix3d_get(Matrix3D *lambda, size_t idx);\n55\t\n56\t/**\n57\t * @brief Get a pointer to a specific row in a 2D matrix.\n58\t *\n59\t * This function 